UNIT isFullwidthCodePoint
KIND FUNCTIONAL
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
SIG isFullwidthCodePoint(codePoint: number) -> boolean
DEPENDS-ON none
# Zero runtime dependencies. Uses only the global Number.isNaN.

BEHAVIOR
# Pure total function of one argument. No seam (no clock/RNG/io/net). No state.
# The function is the package's DEFAULT export. In CJS the source assigns BOTH:
#   module.exports = isFullwidthCodePoint
#   module.exports.default = isFullwidthCodePoint   # the same function object
# The blind re-emitter targets ESM: `export default <fn>` (see SCOPE / ENVELOPE).
#
# Comparisons in the body are RAW JS relational operators (>= <= === !==) applied
# directly to `codePoint`. There is NO Math.floor / integer truncation / |0. A
# non-integer float is therefore tested literally against the numeric bounds (a
# fractional value strictly inside a range returns true; one between ranges returns
# false). This is load-bearing — see edge cases below.
#
# ORDERED PIPELINE:
#
# NODE 1 (NaN guard):
#   if Number.isNaN(codePoint) is true -> return false   # short-circuit, before any range test
#   NB: Number.isNaN (NOT the global isNaN) — no coercion. Only an actual NaN
#       number value triggers this. (undefined/null/strings do NOT reach here as NaN;
#       they fall through to NODE 2 and are out-of-envelope — see ENVELOPE.)
#
# NODE 2 (outer guard + range disjunction):
#   return true  IFF  ( codePoint >= 0x1100 ) AND ( ANY of the range clauses below holds );
#   otherwise (NODE 3) return false.
#
#   The outer guard `codePoint >= 0x1100` gates the ENTIRE disjunction. Everything
#   strictly below 0x1100 (4352) is false regardless of the clauses — including
#   ASCII, 0, negatives. (No clause matches below 0x1100 anyway, but the guard makes
#   it an explicit early exit.)
#
#   RANGE CLAUSES (the disjunction; `cp` = codePoint). A clause is satisfied per
#   ordinary JS relational comparison:
#
#     R1  Hangul Jamo:                  cp <= 0x115F                     # given cp>=0x1100, i.e. [0x1100, 0x115F]
#     S1  singleton:                    cp === 0x2329                    # LEFT-POINTING ANGLE BRACKET
#     S2  singleton:                    cp === 0x232A                    # RIGHT-POINTING ANGLE BRACKET
#     R2  CJK Radicals Supp .. Encl:    0x2E80 <= cp <= 0x3247  AND  cp !== 0x303F
#     R3  Encl CJK .. Ext A:            0x3250 <= cp <= 0x4DBF
#     R4  CJK Unified .. Yi Radicals:   0x4E00 <= cp <= 0xA4C6
#     R5  Hangul Jamo Extended-A:       0xA960 <= cp <= 0xA97C
#     R6  Hangul Syllables:             0xAC00 <= cp <= 0xD7A3
#     R7  CJK Compat Ideographs:        0xF900 <= cp <= 0xFAFF
#     R8  Vertical Forms:               0xFE10 <= cp <= 0xFE19
#     R9  CJK Compat Forms .. Small:    0xFE30 <= cp <= 0xFE6B
#     R10 Halfwidth/Fullwidth Forms:    0xFF01 <= cp <= 0xFF60          # !!! LOWER BOUND IS 0xFF01, NOT 0xFF00 !!!
#     R11 (Fullwidth signs):            0xFFE0 <= cp <= 0xFFE6
#     R12 Kana Supplement:              0x1B000 <= cp <= 0x1B001
#     R13 Enclosed Ideographic Supp:    0x1F200 <= cp <= 0x1F251
#     R14 CJK Ext B .. Tertiary Ideo:   0x20000 <= cp <= 0x3FFFD
#
# NODE 3 (default): return false.
#
# CRITICAL EXACTNESS NOTES (verified by running the real package — see PROVENANCE):
#   * R10 LOWER BOUND IS 0xFF01 (65281), NOT 0xFF00. VERIFIED:
#       isFullwidthCodePoint(0xFF00) === false
#       isFullwidthCodePoint(0xFF01) === true
#     A blind engineer who writes 0xFF00 WILL DIVERGE at 0xFF00. The source line is:
#       (0xFF01 <= codePoint && codePoint <= 0xFF60)
#   * R2 EXCLUDES exactly 0x303F (12351): inside [0x2E80, 0x3247] but masked out by
#       `cp !== 0x303F`. VERIFIED: f(0x303E)=true, f(0x303F)=false, f(0x3040)=true.
#       The !== is a strict equality, so a NON-integer like 0x303F+0.5 (12351.5) is
#       NOT equal to 0x303F and (being in [0x2E80,0x3247]) returns true.
#   * The gap [0x3248, 0x324F] is NOT covered (R2 ends 0x3247, R3 starts 0x3250):
#       f(0x3248)=false, f(0x3249..0x324F)=false, f(0x3250)=true.
#   * The gap [0x4DC0, 0x4DFF] is NOT covered (R3 ends 0x4DBF, R4 starts 0x4E00).
#   * The gap (0xFF60, 0xFFE0) is NOT covered: f(0xFF61)=false.
#   * Return type is a real boolean (typeof === "boolean"), never truthy/falsy other.
#
# FULL BOUNDARY TRUTH TABLE (every range edge +/- 1, verified against real pkg):
#   0x10FF F | 0x1100 T | 0x115F T | 0x1160 F
#   0x2328 F | 0x2329 T | 0x232A T | 0x232B F
#   0x2E7F F | 0x2E80 T | 0x303E T | 0x303F F | 0x3040 T | 0x3247 T | 0x3248 F
#   0x324F F | 0x3250 T | 0x4DBF T | 0x4DC0 F
#   0x4DFF F | 0x4E00 T | 0xA4C6 T | 0xA4C7 F
#   0xA95F F | 0xA960 T | 0xA97C T | 0xA97D F
#   0xABFF F | 0xAC00 T | 0xD7A3 T | 0xD7A4 F
#   0xF8FF F | 0xF900 T | 0xFAFF T | 0xFB00 F
#   0xFE0F F | 0xFE10 T | 0xFE19 T | 0xFE1A F
#   0xFE2F F | 0xFE30 T | 0xFE6B T | 0xFE6C F
#   0xFF00 F | 0xFF01 T | 0xFF60 T | 0xFF61 F
#   0xFFDF F | 0xFFE0 T | 0xFFE6 T | 0xFFE7 F
#   0x1AFFF F | 0x1B000 T | 0x1B001 T | 0x1B002 F
#   0x1F1FF F | 0x1F200 T | 0x1F251 T | 0x1F252 F
#   0x1FFFF F | 0x20000 T | 0x3FFFD T | 0x3FFFE F
#   NaN F | -1 F | -0x1100 F | 65('A') F | 0 F | Infinity F | -Infinity F
#   4352.5 T (in R1) | 4447.5 F (=0x115F+0.5, between R1 and R2) | 1e9 F (> 0x3FFFD)
#   12350.5 T | 12351.5 T (0x303F +/-0.5, !==0x303F, in R2)

ORACLE value -> oracle.json
# Deterministic value oracle: expected = real isFullwidthCodePoint(codePoint), a boolean.

SCOPE
# ALL behavior is IN-CONTRACT LOGIC — reproduce exactly. The function is pure.
# There is NO CARRIED DATA: the range bounds are 14 ranges + 2 singletons + 1
# exclusion, written inline in the SIR above in full (not a large literal table that
# must be extracted byte-exact). A blind engineer reproduces them verbatim from this
# SIR. Therefore NO carried.json is emitted.
# There is NO OUT-OF-CONTRACT behavior (no mutators, no side APIs).
#
# INPUT/OUTPUT ENVELOPE (the contract type is `number` per index.d.ts):
#   IN-ENVELOPE arg values (all round-trip the oracle codec and are emitted by genInputs):
#     - any finite number: integers AND non-integer floats (raw comparisons, no flooring)
#     - negatives, 0
#     - NaN            (codec round-trips NaN; NODE 1 returns false)
#     - +Infinity      (>= 0x1100 true, but no range clause holds -> false)
#     - -Infinity      (>= 0x1100 false -> false)
#     - -0             (codec round-trips -0; behaves as 0 -> false)
#     Huge magnitudes beyond 0x3FFFD -> false (no clause). VERIFIED 1e9 -> false.
#
#   OUT-OF-ENVELOPE / DOCUMENT-AS-OUT (NOT emitted by genInputs; behavior noted for completeness):
#     - non-number arguments (string, null, undefined, boolean, object): the .d.ts
#       types codePoint as `number`. Passing a non-number relies on JS coercion in the
#       relational operators and is OUTSIDE the contract. (Observed: undefined->false,
#       null->false, "5000"->false, but this is incidental coercion, not contract.)
#       These are EXCLUDED from genInputs.
#     - functions and Symbols as arguments: NON-ROUND-TRIPPABLE through the oracle
#       codec (JSON.stringify(encode(args)) corrupts them) AND out-of-contract. A
#       Symbol arg additionally THROWS on relational coercion. EXCLUDED from genInputs;
#       a blind re-emitter still reconstructs the spec without them.
#     - boxed Number (new Number(0x1100)): out-of-contract object; identity does not
#       survive the codec. EXCLUDED from genInputs.

